# Classical electromagnetism audit and expansion

2026-10-03. **All exact declared research branches now have explicit contracts
and complete conditional arguments, examples or qualified primary nonproof
accounts.** This is author/root local review, not independent acceptance or
production certification. No original/import, production item/page/plan, engine
state or publication was changed.

[The exact ledger](closure-ledger.json) preserves every original 177 proposal ID
and adds 40 proposals: 217 total, 152 physical and 65 mathematical. Physical content
has 69 physical theorems, 4 thought experiments, 40 examples, 24 definitions,
10 postulates, 3 reported experiments and 2 scope remarks. Mathematics has
45 lemmas, 8 theorems,8 examples and 4 definitions. There are 18 physical and 10
mathematical A/B pairs; the largest page contains 27 proposals, below 100.

## Complete argument and definition mapping

The ledger maps every proposal ID to its exact definition/formulation or argument.
[Definition contracts](scaffold/definition-contracts.md) specify objects, domains,
regularity, units, transformations, source/boundary support and physical regime.
Mathematical definitions/arguments have mathematical premises only.

[Completed analysis arguments](scaffold/completed-expansion-arguments.md):

- W1–W7: smooth Kirchhoff/Duhamel existence, local cone energy uniqueness and
  finite propagation; retarded kernel; constrained vacuum/forced Maxwell IVP;
  conserved-source retarded potentials and actual gauge reachability.
- R1–R4: uniform-subluminal retarded-root existence, derivatives and delta
  Jacobian; fully differentiated Liénard–Wiechert fields; rest Larmor and
  relativistic emitted power, including its boundary/time conversion.
- S1–S3: smooth Newtonian upgrading, closed thin-current distribution/limit,
  magnetic dipole and differentiated uniform remainder.
- C1–C5,O1: complete tensor/component Maxwell equivalence, covariance, field
  boosts/invariants, observer split/Doppler, relativistic force/work/low-speed
  limit, stress-energy divergence and coupled angular balance.
- V1–V2: complete timelike fixed-endpoint particle and compact field variations,
  with source/gauge continuity and stationary-versus-minimum distinction.
- D1–D3: actual causal integrable response, analytic dispersion, finite
  subtractions and explicit passivity/storage qualifications.
- A1–A2: uniform compact-source far-zone fields/flux and controlled dipole error.
- B1–B7: coercivity/variational solver, actual prescribed trace lifts,
  Dirichlet/compatible Neumann/transmission existence and full smooth-domain
  regularity by difference quotients, normal recovery, induction and embedding.
- H1–H3: convergent kernel, harmonic decomposition, spherical L² basis/addition
  and ball boundary series convergence.
- G1–G3: exact TE/TM modes, rectangular energy completeness and closed smooth
  PEC curl spectral closure with topology zero modes.
- P1–P3,U1–U2: dipole scattering, SR weak-field Thomson, controlled scalar
  source diffraction and conditional bounded-error model comparison.
- E1–E3: primary Faraday/Hertz/Cavendish accounts with explicit source limits.

